{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Reverse-engineering",
  "Notes": "Fit layer thicknesses to a measured reflectance spectrum\n\nCaveats:\n- L2 deliberately: fitting to noisy data is the one case where least squares is the right norm rather than a default, because it is the maximum-likelihood estimate for Gaussian noise. A minimax fit here would chase the worst measurement.\n- No manufacturability term (MINT/MAXT, or SENS), unlike every other example. This is an estimation problem, not a design problem: the thicknesses sought are the ones actually deposited, whatever they are. A thickness penalty would pull the fit away from the truth toward a design somebody would have preferred to build.\n- Only thicknesses are fitted, not the materials\u0027 indices.",
